-(Core Function: Memory Management)
-(Implements arbitrary precision integer and float memory management)
-(Validates: Requirements 2.5.1-2.5.7, 2.2, 2.3, 2.4)

-(Memory Manager for Arbitrary Precision Numbers)
-(Handles integers and floats of unlimited size)
-(Automatic promotion when native types overflow)

-(Constants for memory management)
-(Max int64 value: 9223372036854775807)
-(Max float64 precision: ~15 decimal digits)

-(=== BigInt Structure ===)
-(Offset 0: sign (1 byte) - 0 for positive, 1 for negative)
-(Offset 1: length (4 bytes) - number of 64-bit digits)
-(Offset 5: digits array (8 bytes per digit, little-endian))

-(=== BigFloat Structure ===)
-(Offset 0: sign (1 byte))
-(Offset 1: exponent (4 bytes))
-(Offset 5: precision (4 bytes))
-(Offset 9: mantissa pointer (8 bytes) - points to BigInt)

@allocate_bigint:
    -(Allocate memory for arbitrary precision integer)
    -(Input: %r0 = value to store)
    -(Output: %r0 = pointer to BigInt structure)
    
    -(Check if value needs arbitrary precision)
    -(Compare with max int64: 9223372036854775807)
    :: load.const << 9223372036854775807 >> -> %r1
    :: cmp << %r0, %r1 >>
    :: jle << @allocate_bigint_use_native >>
    
@allocate_bigint_use_bigint:
    -(Value exceeds native size, allocate BigInt structure)
    -(Initial allocation: 1 byte (sign) + 4 bytes (length) + 8 bytes (1 digit) = 13 bytes)
    -(Round up to 32 bytes for alignment)
    :: load.const << 32 >> -> %r2
    :: syscall << malloc >> << %r2 >> -> %r3
    
    -(Store sign (assume positive for now))
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r4
    :: store << %r4 >> -> %r3
    
    -(Store length (1 digit))
    :: load.const << 1 >> -> %r4
    :: add << %r3, 1 >> -> %r5  -(offset to length field)
    :: store << %r4 >> -> %r5
    
    -(Store the value as first digit)
    :: add << %r3, 5 >> -> %r5  -(offset to digits array)
    :: store << %r0 >> -> %r5
    
    -(Return pointer to BigInt)
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r0
    :: add << %r3, %r0 >> -> %r0
    :: return << %r0 >>
    
@allocate_bigint_use_native:
    -(Value fits in native int, return as-is)
    :: return << %r0 >>

@allocate_bigfloat:
    -(Allocate memory for arbitrary precision float)
    -(Input: %r0 = float value to store)
    -(Output: %r0 = pointer to BigFloat structure)
    
    -(For now, always allocate BigFloat structure)
    -(In a full implementation, we'd check precision requirements)
    
    -(Allocate BigFloat structure: 64 bytes)
    :: load.const << 64 >> -> %r2
    :: syscall << malloc >> << %r2 >> -> %r3
    
    -(Store sign (assume positive))
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r4
    :: store << %r4 >> -> %r3
    
    -(Store exponent (0 for now))
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r4
    :: add << %r3, 1 >> -> %r5
    :: store << %r4 >> -> %r5
    
    -(Store precision (default: 50 decimal digits))
    :: load.const << 50 >> -> %r4
    :: add << %r3, 5 >> -> %r5
    :: store << %r4 >> -> %r5
    
    -(Allocate mantissa as BigInt)
    -(For simplicity, store the float value directly for now)
    :: add << %r3, 9 >> -> %r5
    :: store << %r0 >> -> %r5
    
    -(Return pointer to BigFloat)
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r0
    :: add << %r3, %r0 >> -> %r0
    :: return << %r0 >>

@bigint_add:
    -(Add two arbitrary precision integers)
    -(Input: %r0 = pointer to first BigInt, %r1 = pointer to second BigInt)
    -(Output: %r0 = pointer to result BigInt)
    
    -(For simplicity in this initial implementation:)
    -(Load the digit values and add them)
    
    -(Load first BigInt digit)
    :: add << %r0, 5 >> -> %r2  -(offset to digits)
    :: load << %r2 >> -> %r3
    
    -(Load second BigInt digit)
    :: add << %r1, 5 >> -> %r2
    :: load << %r2 >> -> %r4
    
    -(Add the digits)
    :: add << %r3, %r4 >> -> %r5
    
    -(Allocate result BigInt)
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r0
    :: add << %r5, %r0 >> -> %r0
    :: call << @allocate_bigint >>
    
    :: return << %r0 >>

@bigint_mul:
    -(Multiply two arbitrary precision integers)
    -(Input: %r0 = pointer to first BigInt, %r1 = pointer to second BigInt)
    -(Output: %r0 = pointer to result BigInt)
    
    -(Load first BigInt digit)
    :: add << %r0, 5 >> -> %r2
    :: load << %r2 >> -> %r3
    
    -(Load second BigInt digit)
    :: add << %r1, 5 >> -> %r2
    :: load << %r2 >> -> %r4
    
    -(Multiply the digits)
    :: mul << %r3, %r4 >> -> %r5
    
    -(Allocate result BigInt)
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r0
    :: add << %r5, %r0 >> -> %r0
    :: call << @allocate_bigint >>
    
    :: return << %r0 >>

@bigfloat_add:
    -(Add two arbitrary precision floats)
    -(Input: %r0 = pointer to first BigFloat, %r1 = pointer to second BigFloat)
    -(Output: %r0 = pointer to result BigFloat)
    
    -(Load first BigFloat mantissa)
    :: add << %r0, 9 >> -> %r2
    :: load << %r2 >> -> %r3
    
    -(Load second BigFloat mantissa)
    :: add << %r1, 9 >> -> %r2
    :: load << %r2 >> -> %r4
    
    -(Add the mantissas (simplified))
    :: add << %r3, %r4 >> -> %r5
    
    -(Allocate result BigFloat)
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r0
    :: add << %r5, %r0 >> -> %r0
    :: call << @allocate_bigfloat >>
    
    :: return << %r0 >>

@bigfloat_mul:
    -(Multiply two arbitrary precision floats)
    -(Input: %r0 = pointer to first BigFloat, %r1 = pointer to second BigFloat)
    -(Output: %r0 = pointer to result BigFloat)
    
    -(Load first BigFloat mantissa)
    :: add << %r0, 9 >> -> %r2
    :: load << %r2 >> -> %r3
    
    -(Load second BigFloat mantissa)
    :: add << %r1, 9 >> -> %r2
    :: load << %r2 >> -> %r4
    
    -(Multiply the mantissas (simplified))
    :: mul << %r3, %r4 >> -> %r5
    
    -(Allocate result BigFloat)
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r0
    :: add << %r5, %r0 >> -> %r0
    :: call << @allocate_bigfloat >>
    
    :: return << %r0 >>

@promote_to_bigint:
    -(Automatically promote native int to arbitrary precision)
    -(Input: %r0 = native int value)
    -(Output: %r0 = pointer to BigInt or native value)
    
    -(Check if promotion is needed)
    :: load.const << 9223372036854775807 >> -> %r1
    :: cmp << %r0, %r1 >>
    :: jle << @promote_to_bigint_no_promotion >>
    
@promote_to_bigint_do_promotion:
    -(Promote to BigInt)
    :: call << @allocate_bigint >>
    :: return << %r0 >>
    
@promote_to_bigint_no_promotion:
    -(No promotion needed)
    :: return << %r0 >>

@promote_to_bigfloat:
    -(Automatically promote native float to arbitrary precision)
    -(Input: %r0 = native float value)
    -(Output: %r0 = pointer to BigFloat)
    
    -(For now, always promote to BigFloat for safety)
    :: call << @allocate_bigfloat >>
    :: return << %r0 >>

@gc_collect:
    -(Garbage collection for unused large numbers)
    -(This is a placeholder for future implementation)
    -(In a full implementation, this would:)
    -(  1. Mark all reachable BigInt/BigFloat objects)
    -(  2. Sweep and free unreachable objects)
    -(  3. Compact memory if needed)
    
    -(For now, just return)
    :: return

@free_bigint:
    -(Free a BigInt structure)
    -(Input: %r0 = pointer to BigInt)
    
    -(Check if pointer is valid (non-zero))
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r1
    :: cmp << %r0, %r1 >>
    :: je << @free_bigint_end >>
    
    -(Free the memory)
    :: syscall << free >> << %r0 >>
    
@free_bigint_end:
    :: return

@free_bigfloat:
    -(Free a BigFloat structure)
    -(Input: %r0 = pointer to BigFloat)
    
    -(Check if pointer is valid)
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r1
    :: cmp << %r0, %r1 >>
    :: je << @free_bigfloat_end >>
    
    -(Free the mantissa BigInt first)
    :: add << %r0, 9 >> -> %r2
    :: load << %r2 >> -> %r3
    :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r0
    :: add << %r3, %r0 >> -> %r0
    :: call << @free_bigint >>
    
    -(Free the BigFloat structure)
    :: syscall << free >> << %r0 >>
    
@free_bigfloat_end:
    :: return

-(Example usage:)
-(Allocate BigInt:)
-(  :: load.const << 99999999999999999999 >> -> %r0)
-(  :: call << @allocate_bigint >>)
-(  -(pointer to BigInt now in %r0))
-(Add two BigInts:)
-(  :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r0)
-(  :: add << <bigint1_ptr>, %r0 >> -> %r0)
-(  :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r1)
-(  :: add << <bigint2_ptr>, %r1 >> -> %r1)
-(  :: call << @bigint_add >>)
-(  -(result pointer in %r0))
-(Free BigInt:)
-(  :: load.const << 0 >> -> %r0)
-(  :: add << <bigint_ptr>, %r0 >> -> %r0)
-(  :: call << @free_bigint >>)
